  "title": "Filters together",
  "verdict": "One combination holds up: the whole shank's CSD through 10-40 Hz AND 5-100 Hz. On two seeds it flagged 12.1% and 11.6% at the 20% setting against Tooth Fairy's 12.7% and 12.6%, and 3.7% and 2.8% at 30% against 4.7% and 4.3% -- about 100 fewer candidates to look at -- with the same 1.0% of garbage let into DS. The peak-channel trace at 10-40 Hz looked as good on one seed and not on the other, so it is noise; everything else flags more. A second seed moves a row by about a point, which is the size of every difference here: read the table with that in mind."
